cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use VariantCentrifuge in your research, please cite the software
  and record the release or commit used in your analysis.
type: software
title: VariantCentrifuge
abstract: >-
  VariantCentrifuge is a research-use command-line pipeline for filtering,
  extracting, and prioritizing genetic variants from VCF files. It combines
  gene-centric region extraction, multi-tier filtering, inheritance analysis,
  configurable scoring, association testing, and report generation.
version: 0.17.13
url: https://scholl-lab.github.io/variantcentrifuge/
repository-code: https://github.com/scholl-lab/variantcentrifuge
license: MIT
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
  - variant prioritization
  - VCF
  - inheritance analysis
authors:
  - family-names: Popp
    given-names: Bernt
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3679-1081
    affiliation: Berlin Institute of Health at Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin, Center of Functional Genomics, Berlin, Germany; Labor Berlin – Charité Vivantes GmbH, Berlin, Germany
